# Phase 1: User Authentication & Onboarding

Implement user authentication using Clerk and sync user data to the Supabase `users` table.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Clerk Authentication
- Clerk handles Sign Up, Login, Forgot Password, and Email Verification out of the box via the existing `/sign-in` and `/sign-up` routes.
- Social login (Google) must be enabled in your Clerk Dashboard (we cannot configure this via code).

### 2. Onboarding Flow (`/onboarding`)
- **[NEW]** `src/app/onboarding/page.tsx`: A short form presented immediately after the first login to collect `college` and `branch`.
- **[NEW]** `src/actions/user.ts`: A Next.js Server Action that receives the onboarding data and inserts the new user row into the Supabase `users` table.

### 3. Route Protection & Redirects
- **[MODIFY]** `src/middleware.ts`: Ensure `/onboarding` is protected.
- **[MODIFY]** `src/app/dashboard/layout.tsx`: Refactor into a Server Component. It will check if the logged-in Clerk user exists in the Supabase `users` table. If they do not exist, it will redirect them to `/onboarding`.
- **[NEW]** `src/components/DashboardSidebar.tsx`: Extract the interactive client-side sidebar from the current `layout.tsx` so the layout itself can run on the server.

